@code{beads.el} is a Magit-like, keyboard-driven Emacs interface for the
Beads (@command{bd}) issue tracker.  It provides transient menus,
tabulated issue lists, and a VUI-based project board for managing issues,
dependencies, molecules, formulas, agents, and workflows without leaving
Emacs.  It is a porcelain over the @command{bd} command-line tool: every
command drives @command{bd --json} and renders the structured result.

The manual is organized by task.  The @ref{Introduction} explains the
conventions it uses, @ref{Installation and Requirements} sets the
package up, and @ref{Getting Started} walks through a first issue.  The
task chapters (@ref{Issue Workflow}, @ref{Dashboards and Views},
@ref{Formulas Molecules and Epics}, @ref{Agents and Sling},
@ref{Orchestration and Terminal}, and @ref{Maintenance and Extending})
cover the day-to-day and administrative surface.  @ref{Command and
Variable Reference} is the lookup chapter and @ref{Concepts} defines the
vocabulary; the two indexes close the manual.

@menu
* Introduction::                What beads.el is and how to read this manual.
* Installation and Requirements::  What you need and how to install it.
* Getting Started::             Your first issue and the interaction model.
* Issue Workflow::              Create, list, view, edit, close, and label.
* Dashboards and Views::        The board, lists, show, and eldoc.
* Formulas Molecules and Epics:: Formulas, molecules, and epics.
* Agents and Sling::            Agents, backends, sessions, sling, swarm.
* Orchestration and Terminal::  Menus, terminal, Dolt, remotes, audit.
* Maintenance and Extending::   Options, building, plumbing, contributing.
* Command and Variable Reference:: Commands, options, and user options.
* Concepts::                    Stores, issues, dependencies, molecules.
* Key Index::                   Keystrokes.
* Command and Variable Index::  Commands, functions and user options.
@end menu
